JUnit XML is the lingua franca of CI: Jenkins (junit step), GitLab (artifacts:reports:junit), Azure DevOps and GitHub Actions reporters all read it to show test tabs and trends. `pytest --junitxml=reports/junit.xml` writes it; Playwright's test runner and most tools can too. Errors (setup/fixture problems) and failures (assertion failed) are different signals: errors usually mean environment/framework issues, failures usually mean product or test bugs. `root.iter()` works whether the root is `<testsuites>` or a single `<testsuite>`.

